instructions: patch each anchor file (app.txt, other.txt), record the verify command (go test ./...) as verifyCmd in .verdict/state/4291/patch.json, commit and push the fix, re-fetch with fetch acme/app 4291, then run it through verdict verify acme/app 4291 and write verification.json beside it [{sig, verdict, verifyCmd}] with one claim per sig, verdict VERIFIED, and that verifyCmd (a claim flips only on the verify-receipt.json verify writes — exit 0 for that command on the pushed head's content); land it with post acme/app 4291; re-run fix acme/app 4291 --all for the next pass
gate: keep the verify command repo-scoped, non-destructive, and offline — the verify verb refuses destructive/networked/credential-reading/repo-escaping shapes before running anything (typed verify-* errors with a try: hint), so run anything stronger in your own shell — it writes no receipt, so settle that finding with verdict triage
loops multiply agent spend — cap review spend with REVIEW_BUDGET_USD or the typed budget_usd default (see docs/manual.md)
next: patch app.txt, other.txt, commit, push, re-fetch, run verify "go test ./..." through verdict verify, write verification.json, run post to land it, then re-run fix --all
